\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the counting pipeline. VGGT predicts a point map for every view, and SAM3 segments the apples as instance masks. After outlier removal, the masks are matched between all pairs of views and aggregated into multi-view instances, which are checked against a sphere as apple model. In the refined pipeline, instances that are too large are re-associated with stricter thresholds (dashed). The centers of the accepted spheres are clustered to obtain the count.}}{18}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method_pipeline}{{4.1}{18}{Overview of the counting pipeline. VGGT predicts a point map for every view, and SAM3 segments the apples as instance masks. After outlier removal, the masks are matched between all pairs of views and aggregated into multi-view instances, which are checked against a sphere as apple model. In the refined pipeline, instances that are too large are re-associated with stricter thresholds (dashed). The centers of the accepted spheres are clustered to obtain the count}{figure.caption.10}{}}
